    {
      "id": "guest-flow",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 1400,
      "y": -170,
      "w": 1330,
      "text": "Guest flow, left to right: questionnaire (6 steps, ~90s) -> waiting screen with the 24h promise -> published itinerary -> swap a stop.\nThe map is one map for the whole trip: dotted lines carry the drive from the villa. Click a place on it."
    },
    {
      "id": "map-perf",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -170,
      "w": 1280,
      "text": "Every pin x/y and every route path here is precomputed at publish time and baked into published_snapshot. The browser does no projection maths, so this renders as static HTML before any JS runs."
    },
    {
      "id": "reason-codes",
      "page": "page-2",
      "x": 1400,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 1280,
      "text": "The reason-code picker is the whole point of the review step. Every edit writes an itinerary_edits row with before/after JSON and a reason code, and those codes are the labels that drive the next prompt version."
    },
    {
      "id": "tokens-note",
      "page": "page-3",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 1180,
      "text": "These are matched to Lohono's ivory / ink / brass / forest look, not lifted from their stylesheet. They live in one file (apps/web/src/lib/tokens.css), so exact brand hexes are a one-file swap."
